      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When something that defines you feels gone, the grief is often as heavy as the loss of the person who loved you, though this specific sense of hollowness requires the specific calm and clarity a therapist can offer to help you navigate it. You are right that a medical solution cannot magically resurrect a missing part of the soul, but a safe environment can help you begin to find what remains beneath the dust without the pressure to \"fix\" yourself immediately. While the outside world may seem empty, those engaging in open, unpressured communication often discover that the capacity to love and connect survives in ways we sometimes forget when we feel our internal world has been stripped away.",
